cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:38:This note covers three game-neutral changes to Isaiah's trainer on the clean base, serving the
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:39:[[../decisions/restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base|restart Decision]]. They are rebuild Task 3.1, Task 3.6 and the Phase 4 `TeacherTargets` refactor in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/plan.md`. They follow principle I11 (refactor, don't add shims). Kaggriculture types don't exist yet, so each change is proven on Isaiah's Orbit types. A cookbook search found the requirement in the
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:74:| Phase 4 prep | collection `ImportError` | 25 passed; Isaiah's 18 teacher tests pass | 924 passed, 3 skipped |
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:80:- **3.1:** the oracle is an extracted successful-path copy of Isaiah's 32b3ec9 helpers inside the test file, not a literal freeze: its tensor field list derives from the current `ObsBatch` schema, and its copy helper omits the original validation. It checks successful calls only. The Orbit cases (3 seeds × optional fields set/unset × 3 action-mask types) passing against the old helpers in the red run is what validates the oracle. A test-local batch type with different field names round-trips through every helper, and a monkeypatched accelerator transfer shows the no-clone path.
cookbook/references/reward-reuse-preserves-objective-and-critic-semantics.md:42:Owner asks “你有沒有加econ shaping (0.2)?” before the half-hour run. The preceding verification run used unshaped terminal W/L/D; implementation availability did not mean it was enabled. Both GPU recipes now explicitly use W=.2, starvation/drought weights4/1, death cap.25, ineffective weight0, gamma1 and terminal scale.75. The .2 value is the event coefficient, not the cap or an extra own-bank bonus. Bank-based evaluation/promotion remains unchanged. A bounded two-GPU run confirmed nonzero shaping (max step reward .25, zero-sum mean 0); its receipt is `ops/default4096-2026-09-29/results.md`. That establishes execution, not learning benefit. The Isaiah-aligned critic (per-player winner softmax, value 2p − 1) is compatible with this recipe because `terminal_scale = 1 - caps` keeps returns in [-1, 1].
cookbook/references/index.md:5:- [[kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe|Kaggriculture configs follow Isaiah's scaling_6m recipe]] — Task 3.4: 2-rank 128/8, 4-rank 64/4 and 8-rank 32/2 configs deliberately keep scaling_6m's global batch, optimizer, PPO, teacher and compile settings; they load through the real FullConfig with a typed KaggricultureEnvConfig; run_ppo startup checks every forward against the model's GEMM chunking before allocation, prints bounded headroom, then stops explicitly because no Kaggriculture env is wired yet.
cookbook/references/index.md:6:- [[kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic|Kaggriculture model joins Isaiah's factory, trunk compile and masked critic]]: Task 3.1 model side puts the model in `ModelConfig` and `create_model` with game-checked specs. It dispatches trunk compile through a nominal `TrunkCompileAPI`, which compiles only the blocks behind `_run_trunk`'s guard, and it masks the winner softmax as Isaiah does. CPU tests only, Codex r1 found no functional defect; `FullConfig` now pairs it with the Task 3.4 `KaggricultureEnvConfig`.
cookbook/references/index.md:17:- [[full-turn-intentions-coordinate-batched-action-heads|Full-turn intentions coordinate batched action heads]] — Optional U/A hypothesis; Isaiah and the current model already retain shared scratch/plan context. No demonstrated need or cost-benefit for a dedicated coordinator.
cookbook/references/index.md:19:- [[starter-history-and-knowledge-remain-retrievable|Starter history and knowledge remain retrievable]] — The Isaiah source history/license, redirected remotes and selective cookbook lifecycle are retained with explicit verification limits.
cookbook/references/index.md:20:- [[shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop|Shared PPO adapts game batches without a second loop]] — One shared Isaiah PPO trainer carries Kaggriculture batches; its core is upstream-equivalent, the recipe is partially aligned, and teacher, cadence, CUDA-fault and GPU-qualification gaps are tracked in ops. Historical SPS measurements link to their receipts.
cookbook/references/index.md:25:- [[kaggriculture-encoder-reuses-isaiah-stateless-layers|Kaggriculture encoder reuses Isaiah's stateless layers]] — The rebuilt encoder uses Isaiah's StatelessTransformerV1 classes, token roles, packing, compile hook and initialization; only stem input widths are game-specific, and guards chunk both the padded and packed compiled GEMMs below 2^31. Describes the current tree; registration and the masked critic are in the Task 3.1 model-side Reference.
cookbook/references/index.md:26:- [[kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection|Kaggriculture grammar heads sit behind Isaiah's actor projection]] — Task 2.3 adds the 3D→D actor projection and batched grammar heads with exact coupled-Gumbel HIRE sampling, same-path replay with support/length/canonical flags and one host check, head GEMM-extent chunking, and a 6,252,223-parameter preset; synthetic grammar tables stand in until the Task 1.4 binding exposes the Task 1.2 native tables (which exist and match the stand-in bit-for-bit). Describes the current tree.
cookbook/references/full-turn-intentions-coordinate-batched-action-heads.md:4:description: "Optional sampled-intention hypothesis, not a required coordinator: Isaiah and the current model already share scratch/plan context; necessity and cost-benefit remain unproved."
