    48	- **Batch-size option (corrected 2026-09-29).** `winner_ce_6m` is **not** an Isaiah-aligned fallback for Kaggriculture. Relative to `scaling_6m`, `configs/winner_ce_6m.yaml` changes `rl.value_loss` to `winner_ce`, requires `env.reward_mode: win_only` and `value_mode: win_only` (model `stateless_transformer_6m_win_only`), uses a different LR schedule (warmup 200, decay 150,000, `lr_min_ratio` 0.02) and muon weight decay 0.05, and also sets `max_entities` 256, `two_player_weight` 0.5 and teacher chunk 256; its header calls it a value-loss ablation of `baseline.yaml`. Our economic reward is not a winner distribution, and the merged Task 3.2/3.4 guards in `python/owl/train/config.py` reject `winner_ce` and any reward mode other than `win_loss`. Two variants are recorded; neither is adopted:
    49	  - **(c1) Full `winner_ce_6m` recipe:** a reward-design change (win-only reward, winner cross-entropy critic, its own schedule). It needs an owner decision and would reopen the reward and critic semantics, not just the config.
    50	  - **(c2) Batch shape only:** 512 envs × horizon 128, spm 32 (64 envs/rank, spm 4 at 8 ranks) on `scaling_6m` settings. This matches neither Isaiah recipe: each of the 16 optimizer steps per iteration sees 4,096 transitions instead of 1,024 (65,536 per iteration instead of 16,384) under `scaling_6m`'s step-defined schedule. It is a recipe deviation, so adopting it requires a measured comparison against the divided `scaling_6m` shape (complete-work throughput and learning at equal env steps), recorded in the [[recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation|alignment Decision]]. Low GPU utilization at 32 envs/rank is the trigger to measure, not a reason to switch.

